 12.0745 3.52453 11.8926L3.6173 11.6621C3.71685 11.4352 3.83766 11.2176 3.97765 11.0127L4.15343 10.7783C4.34386 10.5462 4.58164 10.312 4.90538 9.98829L11.1964 3.6963L11.3312 3.56837ZM5.84581 10.9287C5.49664 11.2779 5.31252 11.4634 5.18663 11.6162L5.07531 11.7627C4.98188 11.8995 4.90151 12.0448 4.83507 12.1963L4.77355 12.3506C4.73321 12.4607 4.70242 12.5761 4.66808 12.7451L4.54113 13.4619L4.14269 15.8555L4.14171 15.8574H4.14464L6.5382 15.458L7.25499 15.332C7.424 15.2977 7.5394 15.2669 7.64953 15.2266L7.80285 15.165C7.95455 15.0986 8.09947 15.0174 8.23644 14.9238L8.3839 14.8135C8.53668 14.6876 8.72225 14.5035 9.0714 14.1543L14.0587 9.16602L10.8331 5.94044L5.84581 10.9287ZM15.3634 4.63673C14.5281 3.80141 13.2057 3.74938 12.3097 4.48048L12.1368 4.63673L11.7735 5.00001L15.0001 8.22559L15.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="0f1df800-679a-4b0d-a9db-4be9edb36bcc" data-testid="conversation-turn-10" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="0f1df800-679a-4b0d-a9db-4be9edb36bcc" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="172">What you saw on Facebook captures exactly what we were just noticing in those 1950s texts: the rhetoric hasn’t changed much, but the <strong data-start="133" data-end="169">stakes have scaled up enormously</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="174" data-end="415">In the 1950s people worried about whether computers could really “think.” Today the anxiety has shifted to whether AI systems can fairly and transparently <strong data-start="329" data-end="358">judge, decide, and govern</strong>. A few layers to what’s happening in your friend’s case:</p>
<hr data-start="417" data-end="420">
<h3 data-start="422" data-end="452">1. Automated Enforcement</h3>
<p data-start="453" data-end="528">Platforms like Facebook rely on large-scale automated moderation systems:</p>
<ul data-start="529" data-end="840">
<li data-start="529" data-end="596">
<p data-start="531" data-end="596">Algorithms scan for banned content, behaviors, or associations.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="597" data-end="708">
<p data-start="599" data-end="708">If the system flags an account, it can impose suspensions or bans without a human ever looking at the case.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="709" data-end="840">
<p data-start="711" data-end="840">Human review is often promised but rarely delivered, because staffing every appeal would be too expensive at billions of users.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="842" data-end="941">So the “AI” isn’t conscious, but it is acting as a <strong data-start="893" data-end="920">bureaucratic gatekeeper</strong>, with no recourse.</p>
<hr data-start="943" data-end="946">
<h3 data-start="948" data-end="979">2. Black Mirror Parallels</h3>
<p data-start="980" data-end="1043">The “episode of Black Mirror” feeling comes from two factors:</p>
<ul data-start="1044" data-end="1292">
<li data-start="1044" data-end="1148">
<p data-start="1046" data-end="1148"><strong data-start="1046" data-end="1057">Opacity</strong>: you don’t know what rule was broken, what evidence was weighed, or how to challenge it.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1149" data-end="1292">
<p data-start="1151" data-end="1292"><strong data-start="1151" data-end="1165">Dependency</strong>: accounts are tied to social life, work, even identity verification. Losing access feels like losing a piece of one’s world.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1294" data-end="1379">That combination — opaque decision + high dependence — produces the dystopian vibe.</p>
<hr data-start="1381" data-end="1384">
<h3 data-start="1386" data-end="1427">3. The Old “Brain Analogy” Reversed</h3>
<p data-start="1428" data-end="1846">Back in 1955, books warned: “don’t treat the computer as a black box brain — it’s just a machine.”<br data-start="1526" data-end="1529">
Now, the computer has been put in the role of a <strong data-start="1577" data-end="1606">judge of human legitimacy</strong> — and we’re told to treat its judgment as binding, even though it still isn’t “thinking in the creative and associative sense.” The <strong data-start="1739" data-end="1769">category error has flipped</strong>: instead of over-crediting intelligence, we’re over-crediting <em data-start="1832" data-end="1843">authority</em>.</p>
<hr data-start="1848" data-end="1851">
<h3 data-start="1853" data-end="1881">4. Why It Feels “Evil”</h3>
<p data-start="1882" data-end="1926">It isn’t personal malice; it’s structural:</p>
<ul data-start="1927" data-end="2054">
<li data-start="1927" data-end="1967">
<p data-start="1929" data-end="1967">The company wants scale at low cost.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1968" data-end="2004">
<p data-start="1970" data-end="2004">Automation replaces due process.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2005" data-end="2054">
<p data-start="2007" data-end="2054">Accountability is externalized onto the user.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2056" data-end="2165">That’s why it feels like a betrayal: the system that claims to serve you actually treats you as disposable.</p>
<hr data-start="2167" data-end="2170">
<p data-start="2172" data-end="2532" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to give you a <strong data-start="2204" data-end="2231">historical through-line</strong> that ties the 1950s “automatic computers” discussion (machines can’t really think, only follow instructions) directly to today’s situation (machines can’t really judge, yet they are <em data-start="2414" data-end="2423">treated</em> as if they can)? That might crystallize why the feeling of “pure evil” resonates so strongly across decades.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29