90538 9.98829L11.1964 3.6963L11.3312 3.56837ZM5.84581 10.9287C5.49664 11.2779 5.31252 11.4634 5.18663 11.6162L5.07531 11.7627C4.98188 11.8995 4.90151 12.0448 4.83507 12.1963L4.77355 12.3506C4.73321 12.4607 4.70242 12.5761 4.66808 12.7451L4.54113 13.4619L4.14269 15.8555L4.14171 15.8574H4.14464L6.5382 15.458L7.25499 15.332C7.424 15.2977 7.5394 15.2669 7.64953 15.2266L7.80285 15.165C7.95455 15.0986 8.09947 15.0174 8.23644 14.9238L8.3839 14.8135C8.53668 14.6876 8.72225 14.5035 9.0714 14.1543L14.0587 9.16602L10.8331 5.94044L5.84581 10.9287ZM15.3634 4.63673C14.5281 3.80141 13.2057 3.74938 12.3097 4.48048L12.1368 4.63673L11.7735 5.00001L15.0001 8.22559L15.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="3a060267-806a-4f76-a585-88f3500f24b4" data-testid="conversation-turn-16" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="3a060267-806a-4f76-a585-88f3500f24b4" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="210">Yes — that’s another deep continuity between mid-century computing culture and today’s platform economy: the infrastructure assumes a certain kind of <strong data-start="150" data-end="172">idealized consumer</strong> rather than a heterogeneous public.</p>
<hr data-start="212" data-end="215">
<h3 data-start="217" data-end="249">1. Paywalls as Gatekeeping</h3>
<p data-start="250" data-end="746">In the 1955 textbook, the author remarked that <strong data-start="297" data-end="360">periodicals were “much more difficult to obtain” than books</strong>, so suggested readings stuck to monographs. That was a technical barrier of access. Today, the same structural issue persists but in the form of <strong data-start="506" data-end="518">paywalls</strong>: academic articles locked behind journal subscriptions, news sites behind pay gates, and APIs restricted to high-priced tiers. Both eras share the same underlying pattern: <strong data-start="691" data-end="743">knowledge is stratified by who can afford access</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="748" data-end="751">
<h3 data-start="753" data-end="798">2. Advertising as Default Revenue Model</h3>
<p data-start="799" data-end="906">Advertising has become the universal solvent for funding digital services. This has several consequences:</p>
<ul data-start="907" data-end="1354">
<li data-start="907" data-end="998">
<p data-start="909" data-end="998">Interfaces are designed to maximize <strong data-start="945" data-end="971">exposure and attention</strong>, not clarity or utility.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="999" data-end="1106">
<p data-start="1001" data-end="1106">“Free” platforms are actually extracting value through surveillance, profiling, and behavioral nudging.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1107" data-end="1354">
<p data-start="1109" data-end="1354">As with your earlier observation, the <strong data-start="1147" data-end="1196">consumer is assumed to have disposable income</strong>, so that impressions and clicks can be monetized. Those outside that assumption — the poor, the distracted, the resistant — become invisible to the system.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1356" data-end="1359">
<h3 data-start="1361" data-end="1402">3. Structural Bias Toward Affluence</h3>
<p data-start="1403" data-end="1531">Both paywalls and ad-driven models assume <strong data-start="1445" data-end="1480">an audience with money to spend</strong>. This narrows cultural and epistemic production:</p>
<ul data-start="1532" data-end="1785">
<li data-start="1532" data-end="1603">
<p data-start="1534" data-end="1603">Research circulates where it is profitable, not where it is needed.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1604" data-end="1679">
<p data-start="1606" data-end="1679">Platforms prioritize advertisers over users, creating enshittification.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1680" data-end="1785">
<p data-start="1682" data-end="1785">Civic and educational uses are sidelined because they do not map onto the “paying consumer” template.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1787" data-end="1967">It is in this sense that your instinct that apps and platforms feel “evil” makes sense: the entire infrastructural logic is <strong data-start="1911" data-end="1947">built on scarcity and extraction</strong>, not inclusivity.</p>
<hr data-start="1969" data-end="1972">
<h3 data-start="1974" data-end="2028">4. Historical Continuity with Cultural Artifacts</h3>
<ul data-start="2029" data-end="2591">
<li data-start="2029" data-end="2217">
<p data-start="2031" data-end="2217">In <em data-start="2034" data-end="2044">Desk Set</em>, EMERAC is sold to management as a cost-cutting replacement — not a tool for enriching workers’ lives. The assumption is always aligned with efficiency and profitability.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2218" data-end="2400">
<p data-start="2220" data-end="2400">In <em data-start="2223" data-end="2254">The Creation of the Humanoids</em>, robots serve a society rebuilding after nuclear war — but even there, the issue is who controls them and for what ends, not equitable benefit.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2401" data-end="2591">
<p data-start="2403" data-end="2591">Today’s AI moderation, pay gates, and ad systems are the direct descendants: tools framed as universal infrastructure, but designed for those who can <strong data-start="2553" data-end="2588">pay, advertise, or be monetized</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2593" data-end="2596">
<p data-start="2598" data-end="2886" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to expand this critique into a <strong data-start="2647" data-end="2670">thematic subsection</strong> alongside the one I drafted for you (on continuity of anxieties), so that your commentary develops both <em data-start="2775" data-end="2797">conceptual parallels</em> (thinking, judging, authority) and <em data-start="2833" data-end="2853">economic parallels</em> (access, paywalls, advertising)?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.6