<p data-start="397" data-end="588">Here’s a merged <strong data-start="413" data-end="432">working outline</strong> that draws on both the cultural-historical arc (1950s → platforms → chokepoints) and the formal RSVP/semantic infrastructure framework from your monograph:</p>
<hr data-start="590" data-end="593">
<h2 data-start="595" data-end="676">Outline: <em data-start="607" data-end="676">From Gossip to Chokepoint Capitalism: Cycles of Semantic Constraint</em></h2>
<h3 data-start="678" data-end="696"><strong data-start="682" data-end="694">Abstract</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="697" data-end="1083">
<li data-start="697" data-end="875">
<p data-start="699" data-end="875">State the thesis: infrastructures that stabilize meaning (gossip, religion, platforms, chokepoint capitalism) follow a recurring cycle of innovation → ossification → capture.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="876" data-end="930">
<p data-start="878" data-end="930">Show how AI/containerization exemplify this cycle.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="931" data-end="1083">
<p data-start="933" data-end="1083">Argue RSVP/semantic infrastructures provide a new path: entropy-respecting systems that metabolize constraint rather than collapse into chokepoints.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1085" data-end="1088">
<h3 data-start="1090" data-end="1112"><strong data-start="1094" data-end="1110">Introduction</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1113" data-end="1368">
<li data-start="1113" data-end="1194">
<p data-start="1115" data-end="1194">Cultural anxiety: machines as judges (1950s → Facebook bans → generative AI).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1195" data-end="1298">
<p data-start="1197" data-end="1298">Frame the cycle: each infrastructure initially reduces entropy, then becomes a semantic chokepoint.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1299" data-end="1368">
<p data-start="1301" data-end="1368">Preview: essay will move historically, then theoretically (RSVP).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1370" data-end="1373">
<h3 data-start="1375" data-end="1421"><strong data-start="1379" data-end="1419">1. The Early Frame (1950s Textbooks)</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1422" data-end="1668">
<li data-start="1422" data-end="1536">
<p data-start="1424" data-end="1536">Ned Chapin (1963) <em data-start="1442" data-end="1463">Automatic Computers</em> on preprocessing and human labor<span class="" data-state="closed"><span class="relative inline-flex items-center"><button class="ms-1 flex h-[25px] text-[10px] leading-[13px] rounded-xl items-center justify-center gap-1 px-2 relative text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" alt="File" class="h-[12px] w-[12px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M11.2598 2.25191C11.8396 2.25191 12.2381 2.24808 12.6201 2.33981L12.8594 2.40719C13.0957 2.48399 13.3228 2.5886 13.5352 2.71871L13.6582 2.79879C13.9416 2.99641 14.1998 3.25938 14.5586 3.61813L15.5488 4.60836L15.833 4.89449C16.0955 5.16136 16.2943 5.38072 16.4482 5.6318L16.5703 5.84957C16.6829 6.07074 16.7691 6.30495 16.8271 6.54684L16.8574 6.69137C16.918 7.0314 16.915 7.39998 16.915 7.90719V13.0839C16.915 13.7728 16.9157 14.3301 16.8789 14.7802C16.8461 15.1808 16.781 15.5417 16.6367 15.8779L16.5703 16.0205C16.3049 16.5413 15.9008 16.9772 15.4053 17.2812L15.1865 17.4033C14.8099 17.5951 14.4041 17.6745 13.9463 17.7119C13.4961 17.7487 12.9391 17.749 12.25 17.749H7.75C7.06092 17.749 6.50395 17.7487 6.05371 17.7119C5.65317 17.6791 5.29227 17.6148 4.95606 17.4707L4.81348 17.4033C4.29235 17.1378 3.85586 16.7341 3.55176 16.2382L3.42969 16.0205C3.23787 15.6439 3.15854 15.2379 3.12109 14.7802C3.08432 14.3301 3.08496 13.7728 3.08496 13.0839V6.91695C3.08496 6.228 3.08433 5.67086 3.12109 5.22066C3.1585 4.76296 3.23797 4.35698 3.42969 3.98043C3.73311 3.38494 4.218 2.90008 4.81348 2.59664C5.19009 2.40484 5.59593 2.32546 6.05371 2.28805C6.50395 2.25126 7.06091 2.25191 7.75 2.25191H11.2598ZM7.75 3.58199C7.03896 3.58199 6.54563 3.58288 6.16211 3.61422C5.78642 3.64492 5.575 3.70168 5.41699 3.78219C5.0718 3.95811 4.79114 4.23874 4.61524 4.58395C4.53479 4.74193 4.47795 4.95354 4.44727 5.32906C4.41595 5.71254 4.41504 6.20609 4.41504 6.91695V13.0839C4.41504 13.7947 4.41594 14.2884 4.44727 14.6718C4.47798 15.0472 4.53477 15.259 4.61524 15.417L4.68555 15.5429C4.86186 15.8304 5.11487 16.0648 5.41699 16.2187L5.54688 16.2744C5.69065 16.3258 5.88016 16.3636 6.16211 16.3867C6.54563 16.418 7.03898 16.4189 7.75 16.4189H12.25C12.961 16.4189 13.4544 16.418 13.8379 16.3867C14.2135 16.356 14.425 16.2992 14.583 16.2187L14.709 16.1474C14.9963 15.9712 15.2308 15.7189 15.3848 15.417L15.4414 15.2861C15.4927 15.1425 15.5297 14.953 15.5527 14.6718C15.5841 14.2884 15.585 13.7947 15.585 13.0839V8.55758L13.3506 8.30953C12.2572 8.18804 11.3976 7.31827 11.2881 6.22359L11.0234 3.58199H7.75ZM12.6113 6.09176C12.6584 6.56193 13.0275 6.93498 13.4971 6.98727L15.5762 7.21871C15.5727 7.13752 15.5686 7.07109 15.5615 7.01266L15.5342 6.85738C15.5005 6.7171 15.4501 6.58135 15.3848 6.45309L15.3145 6.32711C15.2625 6.24233 15.1995 6.16135 15.0928 6.04488L14.6084 5.54879L13.6182 4.55856C13.2769 4.21733 13.1049 4.04904 12.9688 3.94234L12.8398 3.8525C12.7167 3.77705 12.5853 3.71637 12.4482 3.67184L12.3672 3.6484L12.6113 6.09176Z"></path></svg><p class="not-prose mt-0! mb-0! flex-auto truncate">Semantic Infrastructure</p></button></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1537" data-end="1598">
<p data-start="1539" data-end="1598">Berkeley’s <em data-start="1550" data-end="1564">Giant Brains</em> vs. Turing’s thinking machines.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1599" data-end="1668">
<p data-start="1601" data-end="1668">Lesson: intelligence ascribed too early to deterministic systems.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1670" data-end="1673">
<h3 data-start="1675" data-end="1720"><strong data-start="1679" data-end="1718">2. Cultural Imaginaries (1957–1962)</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1721" data-end="1941">
<li data-start="1721" data-end="1778">
<p data-start="1723" data-end="1778"><em data-start="1723" data-end="1733">Desk Set</em> (1957): EMERAC as a threat vs. complement.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1779" data-end="1864">
<p data-start="1781" data-end="1864"><em data-start="1781" data-end="1812">The Creation of the Humanoids</em> (1962): leap from assistant to authority machine.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1865" data-end="1941">
<p data-start="1867" data-end="1941">These films echo Chapin’s framing: black-box authority vs. human nuance.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1943" data-end="1946">
<h3 data-start="1948" data-end="1984"><strong data-start="1952" data-end="1982">3. Platforms as Enclosures</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1985" data-end="2177">
<li data-start="1985" data-end="2048">
<p data-start="1987" data-end="2048">From scarce institutional computers → ubiquitous platforms.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2049" data-end="2104">
<p data-start="2051" data-end="2104">Example: Facebook bans as opaque machine judgments.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2105" data-end="2177">
<p data-start="2107" data-end="2177">Platforms as gossip at planetary scale: compress, codify, constrain.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2179" data-end="2182">
<h3 data-start="2184" data-end="2218"><strong data-start="2188" data-end="2216">4. Chokepoint Capitalism</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2219" data-end="2470">
<li data-start="2219" data-end="2354">
<p data-start="2221" data-end="2354">Jerry Neumann’s “AI as containerization” analogy: not PC-like (distributed tinkering), but shipping-like (instant commodification).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2355" data-end="2416">
<p data-start="2357" data-end="2416">Few incumbents capture value; entrepreneurs hollowed out.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2417" data-end="2470">
<p data-start="2419" data-end="2470">Consumers benefit, but profit pools dry upstream.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2472" data-end="2475">
<h3 data-start="2477" data-end="2521"><strong data-start="2481" data-end="2519">5. Continuity of Constraint Cycles</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2522" data-end="2728">
<li data-start="2522" data-end="2552">
<p data-start="2524" data-end="2552">Gossip → reputation traps.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2553" data-end="2574">
<p data-start="2555" data-end="2574">Religion → dogma.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2575" data-end="2608">
<p data-start="2577" data-end="2608">Platforms → enshittification.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2609" data-end="2657">
<p data-start="2611" data-end="2657">Containerization/AI → chokepoint capitalism.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2658" data-end="2728">
<p data-start="2660" data-end="2728">Pattern: negentropic beginnings collapse into captured equilibria.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2730" data-end="2733">
<h3 data-start="2735" data-end="2781"><strong data-start="2739" data-end="2779">6. RSVP and Semantic Infrastructures</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2782" data-end="3189">
<li data-start="2782" data-end="3091">
<p data-start="2784" data-end="2869">Draw from <em data-start="2794" data-end="2819">Semantic Infrastructure</em> monograph<span class="" data-state="closed"><span class="relative inline-flex items-center"><button class="ms-1 flex h-[25px] text-[10px] leading-[13px] rounded-xl items-center justify-center gap-1 px-2 relative text-token-text-secondary! hover:text-token-text-primary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" alt="File" class="h-[12px] w-[12px] object-contain text-token-text-primary! flex-none"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M11.2598 2.25191C11.8396 2.25191 12.2381 2.24808 12.6201 2.33981L12.8594 2.40719C13.0957 2.48399 13.3228 2.5886 13.5352 2.71871L13.6582 2.79879C13.9416 2.99641 14.1998 3.25938 14.5586 3.61813L15.5488 4.60836L15.833 4.89449C16.0955 5.16136 16.2943 5.38072 16.4482 5.6318L16.5703 5.84957C16.6829 6.07074 16.7691 6.30495 16.8271 6.54684L16.8574 6.69137C16.918 7.0314 16.915 7.39998 16.915 7.90719V13.0839C16.915 13.7728 16.9157 14.3301 16.8789 14.7802C16.8461 15.1808 16.781 15.5417 16.6367 15.8779L16.5703 16.0205C16.3049 16.5413 15.9008 16.9772 15.4053 17.2812L15.1865 17.4033C14.8099 17.5951 14.4041 17.6745 13.9463 17.7119C13.4961 17.7487 12.9391 17.749 12.25 17.749H7.75C7.06092 17.749 6.50395 17.7487 6.05371 17.7119C5.65317 17.6791 5.29227 17.6148 4.95606 17.4707L4.81348 17.4033C4.29235 17.1378 3.85586 16.7341 3.55176 16.2382L3.42969 16.0205C3.23787 15.6439 3.15854 15.2379 3.12109 14.7802C3.08432 14.3301 3.08496 13.7728 3.08496 13.0839V6.91695C3.08496 6.228 3.08433 5.67086 3.12109 5.22066C3.1585 4.76296 3.23797 4.35698 3.42969 3.98043C3.73311 3.38494 4.218 2.90008 4.81348 2.59664C5.19009 2.40484 5.59593 2.32546 6.05371 2.28805C6.50395 2.25126 7.06091 2.25191 7.75 2.25191H11.2598ZM7.75 3.58199C7.03896 3.58199 6.54563 3.58288 6.16211 3.61422C5.78642 3.