med tightly to follow from the theorem:</p>
<hr data-start="67" data-end="70">
<h3 data-start="72" data-end="106">Corollary (Chokepoint Bots).</h3>
<p data-start="107" data-end="353">When semantic infrastructures suppress or erase obstruction data rather than preserving it, conversations and artworks collapse into <em data-start="240" data-end="257">chokepoint bots</em>: generative processes constrained not by the richness of context but by enforced bottlenecks.</p>
<hr data-start="355" data-end="358">
<h4 data-start="360" data-end="381">Justification.</h4>
<ol data-start="383" data-end="1337">
<li data-start="383" data-end="607">
<p data-start="386" data-end="607"><strong data-start="386" data-end="418">Suppression of obstructions.</strong><br data-start="418" data-end="421">
If a presheaf of contexts is forced into strict sheafification, contradictions and ambiguities vanish. Gossip becomes rumor-trap, religion becomes dogma, platforms become opaque feeds.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="609" data-end="987">
<p data-start="612" data-end="987"><strong data-start="612" data-end="639">Collapsed generativity.</strong><br data-start="639" data-end="642">
In this case, conversations no longer sample from the full functorial model of context but from a reduced projection—outputs determined by which contradictions were erased. Artworks likewise cease to operate as endomorphisms in a rich category of models and instead become finite templates (formulaic genres, algorithmic recommendation slots).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="989" data-end="1337">
<p data-start="992" data-end="1337"><strong data-start="992" data-end="1018">Chokepoint capitalism.</strong><br data-start="1018" data-end="1021">
At scale, these collapses are economic as well as semantic. Containerization, generative platforms, and other infrastructural chokepoints convert open contexts into fixed pipelines where value flows downstream but capture occurs at bottlenecks. The <em data-start="1270" data-end="1275">bot</em> persists, but now trained not on context but on constraint.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1339" data-end="1342">
<h4 data-start="1344" data-end="1378">Interpretation (RSVP Lens).</h4>
<ul data-start="1379" data-end="1539">
<li data-start="1379" data-end="1431">
<p data-start="1381" data-end="1431"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span>: compressed to a single canonical form.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1432" data-end="1478">
<p data-start="1434" data-end="1478"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>⃗</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.714em;"></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.714em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="accent-body" style="left: -0.2077em;"><span class="overlay" style="height: 0.714em; width: 0.471em;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="0.471em" height="0.714em" viewBox="0 0 471 714" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin" style="width: 0.471em;"><path d="M377 20c0-5.333 1.833-10 5.5-14S391 0 397 0c4.667 0 8.667 1.667 12 5
3.333 2.667 6.667 9 10 19 6.667 24.667 20.333 43.667 41 57 7.333 4.667 11
