3 w-3 rounded-full"></div></div><div class="relative my-1 min-h-6"><div class="relative flex max-w-[calc(0.8*var(--thread-content-max-width,40rem))] origin-top-left flex-col gap-2 overflow-x-clip" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><span class="" data-state="closed"><div class="relative w-full text-start"><div class="flex w-full items-start justify-between text-start flex-col"><button class="flex w-full items-center gap-0.5"><span class=""><span class="flex items-center gap-1 text-start align-middle truncate text-token-text-secondary hover:text-token-text-primary" style="opacity: 1;">Thought for 8s</span></span></button></div></div></span></div></div><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="b2bdde8b-bc53-42f4-a207-c512089432df" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-thinking"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="327">Totally doable now—and way easier than even 2–3 years ago—because the hard parts (story structure, retrieval, video synthesis, and camera math) are basically <strong data-start="158" data-end="173">commodities</strong>. You can glue them together into a generative movie app that (a) picks tropes, and (b) chooses camera moves via a simple <strong data-start="295" data-end="319">relevance-activation</strong> engine.</p>
<p data-start="329" data-end="374">Here’s a compact blueprint you can use today.</p>
<h1 data-start="376" data-end="400">What makes it easy now</h1>
<ul data-start="401" data-end="993">
<li data-start="401" data-end="496">
<p data-start="403" data-end="496"><strong data-start="403" data-end="424">Story scaffolding</strong>: LLMs reliably turn a seed prompt into <em data-start="464" data-end="471">beats</em> (acts → scenes → shots).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="497" data-end="633">
<p data-start="499" data-end="633"><strong data-start="499" data-end="519">Trope ontologies</strong>: Community trope lists / your own CSV become a graph (nodes = tropes, edges = “often co-occurs with”/“subverts”).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="634" data-end="747">
<p data-start="636" data-end="747"><strong data-start="636" data-end="659">Retrieval &amp; scoring</strong>: Off-the-shelf vector DBs + spreading-activation math = “what trope is relevant <em data-start="740" data-end="745">now</em>?”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="748" data-end="861">
<p data-start="750" data-end="861"><strong data-start="750" data-end="769">Video synthesis</strong>: Text-to-video/diffusion or game-engine render paths (Unreal/Unity/Blender) are scriptable.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="862" data-end="993">
<p data-start="864" data-end="993"><strong data-start="864" data-end="881">Camera curves</strong>: Cubic Bézier / Catmull-Rom splines with a small cost function give smooth, filmic trajectories out of the box.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h1 data-start="995" data-end="1029">Minimal architecture (6 modules)</h1>
<ol data-start="1030" data-end="1707">
<li data-start="1030" data-end="1156">
<p data-start="1033" data-end="1156"><strong data-start="1033" data-end="1046">Tropes KG</strong>: a weighted graph with attributes (<code data-start="1082" data-end="1089">genre</code>, <code data-start="1091" data-end="1097">tone</code>, <code data-start="1099" data-end="1118">required_entities</code>, <code data-start="1120" data-end="1134">cliché_score</code>, <code data-start="1136" data-end="1154">duration_min/max</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1157" data-end="1275">
<p data-start="1160" data-end="1275"><strong data-start="1160" data-end="1184">Relevance Activation</strong>: a small engine that lights up nodes given user intent + current beat + entities on stage.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1276" data-end="1357">
<p data-start="1279" data-end="1357"><strong data-start="1279" data-end="1295">Beat Planner</strong>: LLM turns user prompt into <code data-start="1324" data-end="1356">{acts → scenes → shot_intents}</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1358" data-end="1459">
<p data-start="1361" data-end="1459"><strong data-start="1361" data-end="1384">Shot List Generator</strong>: maps selected tropes → concrete shot specs (lens, angle, move, duration).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1460" data-end="1579">
<p data-start="1463" data-end="1579"><strong data-start="1463" data-end="1481">Camera Planner</strong>: chooses a spline path + timing to satisfy the shot spec (continuity, 180° rule, parallax, etc.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1580" data-end="1707">
<p data-start="1583" data-end="1707"><strong data-start="1583" data-end="1595">Renderer</strong>: either (A) emit prompts for a video model, or (B) program a scene graph (Unreal Sequencer/Blender) and render.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h1 data-start="1709" data-end="1755">Relevance Activation Theory (practical form)</h1>
<p data-start="1756" data-end="1877">Think <strong data-start="1762" data-end="1786">spreading activation</strong> over your trope graph, with decay and inhibition so you don’t keep repeating the same gag.</p>
<p data-start="1879" data-end="1930"><strong data-start="1879" data-end="1930">Activation for trope <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6151em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span></span> at scene step <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span></span></span></span>:</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><munder><mrow><mi>α</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>user&nbsp;intent</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder><mrow><mi>β</mi><mtext> </mtext><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>current&nbsp;context</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder><mrow><mi>γ</mi><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>s</mi></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>spread</mtext></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>repetition&nbsp;penalty</mtext></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder><mrow><mi>η</mi><mtext> </mtext><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>incompatibilities</mtext></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_k(t)=\underbrace{\alpha\,U(t)}_{\text{user intent}}+\underbrace{\beta\,C_k(t)}_{\text{current context}}+\underbrace{\gamma \sum_{s} w_{s,t}A_{k-1}(s)}_{\text{spread}}-\underbrace{\delta\,R(t)}_{\text{repetition penalty}}-\underbrace{\eta\,I_k(t)}_{\text{incompatibilities}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; ver