6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-python"><span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># --- 1) Load trope graph and weights ---</span></span><span>
G = load_trope_graph(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"tropes.jsonl"</span></span><span>)  </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># nodes with attrs; edges with w</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># --- 2) Plan beats from user seed ---</span></span><span>
beats = llm_plan_beats(user_prompt)   </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># [ {scene: .., entities: .., mood: ..}, ... ]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># --- 3) Activation state ---</span></span><span>
A_prev = defaultdict(</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">float</span></span><span>)
recent = deque(maxlen=</span><span><span class="hljs-number">6</span></span><span>)

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> k, beat </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">enumerate</span></span><span>(beats):
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># Context features</span></span><span>
    Ck = context_features(beat)  </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># entities, mood, stakes</span></span><span>
    Uk = user_intent_features(user_prompt)

    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># score each trope</span></span><span>
    scores = {}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> G.nodes:
        spread = </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">sum</span></span><span>(G[s].get(t,</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.0</span></span><span>) * A_prev[s] </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> s </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> A_prev)
        rep_pen = repetition_penalty(t, recent)
        incompat = incompatibility_penalty(t, beat)
        scores[t] = (
            </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.4</span></span><span>*Uk[t] + </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.35</span></span><span>*Ck[t] + </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.3</span></span><span>*spread
            - </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.2</span></span><span>*rep_pen - </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.25</span></span><span>*incompat
        )

    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># choose top-N tropes this beat</span></span><span>
    chosen = topk(scores, k=</span><span><span class="hljs-number">3</span></span><span>, exclude=incompatible_with(beat))
    recent.extend(chosen)

    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># --- 4) Turn tropes into shot specs ---</span></span><span>
    shots = []
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> trope </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> chosen:
        shots.append(trope_to_shot_spec(trope, beat))

    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># --- 5) Camera trajectories per shot ---</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> s </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> shots:
        p0 = init_camera_curve(s)  </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># initial spline</span></span><span>
        best = minimize_energy(p0, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">lambda</span></span><span> curve: energy(curve, s))
        render_queue.add(s, best)

    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># update activation for next step (normalize)</span></span><span>
    A_prev = normalize({t: scores[t] </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> chosen})
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="5399" data-end="5626">Where <code data-start="5405" data-end="5423">energy(curve, s)</code> computes continuity/framing/jerk and <strong data-start="5461" data-end="5474">subtracts</strong> a “relevance gain” if the move aligns with trope-affinities (e.g., <code data-start="5542" data-end="5559">reversal_reveal</code> loves slow push-in + foreground occluder → background focus rack).</p>
<h1 data-start="5628" data-end="5661">Why this works (and feels good)</h1>
<ul data-start="5662" data-end="6053">
<li data-start="5662" data-end="5808">
<p data-start="5664" data-end="5808"><strong data-start="5664" data-end="5688">Relevance Activation</strong> gives you <em data-start="5699" data-end="5717">coherent variety</em>: it remembers what you’ve done, spreads to nearby ideas, and avoids cliché via cool-downs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5809" data-end="5918">
<p data-start="5811" data-end="5918"><strong data-start="5811" data-end="5826">Camera cost</strong> is <em data-start="5830" data-end="5850">tiny but cinematic</em>: even a simple jerk penalty + framing term gives pro-looking moves.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5919" data-end="6053">
<p data-start="5921" data-end="6053"><strong data-start="5921" data-end="5943">Swappable renderer</strong>: the same shot spec can drive Unreal Sequencer keyframes, Blender (via Python), or prompts for a video model.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h1 data-start="6055" data-end="6093">Quick extensions you’ll probably add</h1>
<ul data-start="6094" data-end="6548">
<li data-start="6094" data-end="6197">
<p data-start="6096" data-end="6197"><strong data-start="6096" data-end="6120">Entity-aware framing</strong>: compute subject screen boxes over time and penalize occlusions/head-cuts.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6198" data-end="6321">
<p data-start="6200" data-end="6321"><strong data-start="6200" data-end="6217">Emotion ramps</strong>: let the activation weights shift over the act structure (higher <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_r</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5806em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02691em;">w</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0269em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> near the midpoint/reversal).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6322" data-end="6450">
<p data-start="6324" data-end="6450"><strong data-start="6324" data-end="6339">Style packs</strong>: per-genre lens/move priors (e.g., horror = longer lenses + slow arcs; action = shorter lenses + whip-pans).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6451" data-end="6548">
<p data-start="6453" data-end="6548"><strong data-start="6453" data-end="6470">User steering</strong>: sliders for “subvert tropes” vs. “lean in,” and “handheld” vs. “locked-off.”</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6550" data-end="6729" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">If you want, I can turn this into a <strong data-start="6586" data-end="6609">starter repo layout</strong> (files, minimal datasets, and a stubbed camera optimizer) you can drop into Unreal/Blender or a text-to-video workflow.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16