integrates the RSVP framing back into the essay:</p>
<hr data-start="83" data-end="86">
<h3 data-start="88" data-end="104">Conclusion</h3>
<p data-start="106" data-end="423">The debate over automatic computers in the 1950s, the cinematic anxieties of <em data-start="183" data-end="193">Desk Set</em> and <em data-start="198" data-end="229">The Creation of the Humanoids</em>, and today’s frustrations with opaque bans or streaming recommendations all circle the same question: <strong data-start="332" data-end="421">what happens when infrastructures built to stabilize meaning harden into chokepoints?</strong></p>
<p data-start="425" data-end="895">From gossip to religion, from platforms to containerization, the pattern repeats. Each begins as a negentropic innovation — a way to metabolize context and reduce uncertainty. Each then ossifies, collapsing contradictions, suppressing ambiguity, and turning expression into a narrow funnel. Every conversation or artwork is a bot trained on its context; every infrastructure decides whether that training corpus is preserved as living context or reduced to a template.</p>
<p data-start="897" data-end="1422">RSVP theory makes this cycle legible in field-theoretic terms. Scalar density (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span>) carries the semantic corpus, vector flow (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>⃗</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.714em;"></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.714em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="accent-body" style="left: -0.2077em;"><span class="overlay" style="height: 0.714em; width: 0.471em;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="0.471em" height="0.714em" viewBox="0 0 471 714" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin" style="width: 0.471em;"><path d="M377 20c0-5.333 1.833-10 5.5-14S391 0 397 0c4.667 0 8.667 1.667 12 5
3.333 2.667 6.667 9 10 19 6.667 24.667 20.333 43.667 41 57 7.333 4.667 11
10.667 11 18 0 6-1 10-3 12s-6.667 5-14 9c-28.667 14.667-53.667 35.667-75 63
