>
<hr data-start="107" data-end="110">
<p data-start="112" data-end="516"><strong data-start="112" data-end="128">Closing Note</strong><br data-start="128" data-end="131">
Every tool we build to carry meaning risks turning into a chokepoint. From gossip to religion, from Shakespeare’s folios to Netflix’s rows, from the microprocessor to generative models, the cycle repeats. The task ahead is not to stop building bots trained on context, but to design infrastructures that keep context alive—systems that metabolize contradiction instead of erasing it.</p>
<hr data-start="518" data-end="523">
