d-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="e30398d4-bf74-487c-8e79-a938d757cda4" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="118">Here’s a compact <strong data-start="17" data-end="49">diagrammatic schema in prose</strong> for Appendix B, to give readers a bird’s-eye view of the pipeline:</p>
<hr data-start="120" data-end="123">
<h3 data-start="125" data-end="159">Appendix B.1: Conceptual Map</h3>
<p data-start="161" data-end="228">The generative cycle can be summarized as a categorical pipeline:</p>
<ol data-start="230" data-end="1462">
<li data-start="230" data-end="458">
<p data-start="233" data-end="458"><strong data-start="233" data-end="280">Corpus → Context Category (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span></span></span></span>)</strong><br data-start="280" data-end="283">
A body of material (dialogue, tradition, dataset) is formalized as an object <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U \in \mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7224em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span></span></span></span>. Morphisms represent restriction, translation, or embedding of context.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="460" data-end="707">
<p data-start="463" data-end="554"><strong data-start="463" data-end="503">Context → Generative Functor (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span></span></span></span>)</strong><br data-start="503" data-end="506">
A conversation or artwork defines a functor</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="script">M</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F: \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{M},</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">M</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="607" data-end="707">mapping contexts into generative models. Each model <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(U)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> is a bot trained on its local corpus.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="709" data-end="901">
<p data-start="712" data-end="901"><strong data-start="712" data-end="750">Generative Functor → Model Outputs</strong><br data-start="750" data-end="753">
Utterances (conversations) are samples from sections; artworks are endomorphisms of models. Both are outputs conditioned by the chosen context.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="903" data-end="1223">
<p data-start="906" data-end="1026"><strong data-start="906" data-end="934">Outputs → Infrastructure</strong><br data-start="934" data-end="937">
Infrastructures determine whether these outputs preserve or collapse contradictions:</p>
<ul data-start="1030" data-end="1223">
<li data-start="1030" data-end="1125">
<p data-start="1032" data-end="1125"><strong data-start="1032" data-end="1060">Semantic infrastructure:</strong> metabolizes obstructions, keeping <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^*(\mathcal{F}) \neq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6887em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mbin mtight">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.09931em;">F</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1129" data-end="1223">
<p data-start="1131" data-end="1223"><strong data-start="1131" data-end="1161">Chokepoint infrastructure:</strong> erases obstructions, collapsing <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^*(\mathcal{F}) \to 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6887em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mbin mtight">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.09931em;">F</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1225" data-end="1462">
<p data-start="1228" data-end="1314"><strong data-start="1228" data-end="1243">RSVP Fields</strong><br data-start="1243" data-end="1246">
At each stage, the RSVP fields measure the state of the system:</p>
<ul data-start="1318" data-end="1462">
<li data-start="1318" data-end="1361">
