lass="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="133">Great — here’s a draft <strong data-start="23" data-end="45">commentary section</strong> that ties the DeepMind <em data-start="69" data-end="76">LIMIT</em> findings back into your category/sheaf/RSVP formalism:</p>
<hr data-start="135" data-end="138">
<h2 data-start="140" data-end="202">Appendix D: Embeddings, Sheaves, and Obstruction Collapse</h2>
<p data-start="204" data-end="649">The DeepMind paper (<em data-start="224" data-end="285">On the Theoretical Limitations of Embedding-Based Retrieval</em>, Weller et al. 2025) provides a crisp mathematical parallel to the chokepoint dynamics we have tracked through culture and economics. Their proof shows that single-vector embeddings cannot scale to represent the combinatorial richness of query–document relations. In our language: <strong data-start="567" data-end="647">single-vector embeddings collapse obstruction classes into trivial sections.</strong></p>
<h3 data-start="651" data-end="689">D.1 Embeddings as Sheaf Sections</h3>
<p data-start="690" data-end="807">Let <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.09931em;">F</span></span></span></span> be a presheaf assigning to each query–document context the set of possible relevance relations.</p>
<ul data-start="808" data-end="1059">
<li data-start="808" data-end="948">
<p data-start="810" data-end="948">In principle, these local sections may not glue consistently: contradictions arise, different queries demand incompatible document sets.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="949" data-end="1059">
<p data-start="951" data-end="1059">Preserving these contradictions means carrying nontrivial obstruction classes <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^*(\mathcal{F}) \neq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6887em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mbin mtight">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.09931em;">F</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1061" data-end="1312">A single-vector embedding model enforces a global section by mapping all local contexts into <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^d</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8491em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">R</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8491em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">d</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> with dot-product similarity. This is equivalent to <strong data-start="1222" data-end="1250">premature sheafification</strong>: contradictions are erased to guarantee a unique extension.</p>
<h3 data-start="1314" data-end="1367">D.2 The Sign-Rank Bound as Obstruction Collapse</h3>
<p data-start="1368" data-end="1607">The sign-rank bound derived in the DeepMind paper tells us that for fixed <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span></span></span></span>, the number of distinguishable relevance patterns grows only polynomially, while the number of possible patterns grows combinatorially. In categorical terms:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Capacity</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">F</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>vs.</mtext><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mtext>Obstructions</mtext><mo>∼</mo><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Capacity}(\mathcal{F}, d) \sim O(d^3) \quad \text{vs.} \quad \# \text{Obstructions} \sim O(n^2).</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Capacity</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.09931em;">F</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∼</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1141em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">3</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">vs.</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord">#</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Obstructions</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∼</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1141em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1719" data-end="1865">Thus, as corpus size grows, the embedding forces <strong data-start="1768" data-end="1792">obstruction collapse</strong>: multiple distinct query–document patterns are identified as the same.</p>
<h3 data-start="1867" data-end="1896">D.3 RSVP Interpretation</h3>
<ul data-start="1897" data-end="2183">
<li data-start="1897" data-end="1985">
<p data-start="1899" data-end="1985"><strong data-start="1899" data-end="1911"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span></strong>: scalar density of meaning is forcibly compressed into dimension <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1986" data-end="2085">
<p data-start="1988" data-end="2085"><strong data-start="1988" data-end="2003"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>⃗</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.714em;"></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.714em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="accent-body" style="left: -0.2077em;"><span class="overlay" style="height: 0.714em; width: 0.471em;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="0.471em" height="0.714em" viewBox="0 0 471 714" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin" style="width: 0.471em;"><path d="M377 20c0-5.333 1.833-10 5.5-14S391 0 397 0c4.667 0 8.667 1.667 12 5
3.333 2.667 6.667 9 10 19 6.667 24.667 20.333 43.667 41 57 7.333 4.667 11
10.667 11 18 0 6-1 10-3 12s-6.667 5-14 9c-28.667 14.667-53.667 35.667-75 63
-1.333 1.333-3.167 3.5-5.5 6.5s-4 4.833-5 5.5c-1 .667-2.5 1.333-4.5 2s-4.333 1
-7 1c-4.667 0-9.167-1.833-13.5-5.5S337 184 337 178c0-12.667 15.667-32.333 47-59
H213l-171-1c-8.667-6-13-12.333-13-19 0-4.667 4.333-11.333 13-20h359
c-16-25.333-24-45-24-59z"></path></svg></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></strong>: flows of relational meaning are bottlenecked through inner-product similarity.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2086" data-end="2183">
<p data-start="2088" data-end="2183"><strong data-start="2088" data-end="2097"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span></strong>: entropy of unresolved contradictions is expelled; embeddings cannot metabolize it.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2185" data-end="2374">This is the precise RSVP analogue of chokepoint capitalism: a system that could in principle preserve obstructions collapses them for the sake of efficiency, creating <strong data-start="2352" data-end="2371">chokepoint bots</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start="2376" data-end="2417">D.4 Towards Semantic Infrastructure</h3>
<p data-start="2418" data-end="2878">BM25 and other sparse/high-dimensional approaches correspond to infrastructures that allow contradictions to persist. In sheaf terms, they do not enforce global uniqueness; in RSVP terms, they maintain nonzero entropy <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span>. Future research in retrieval can be framed as a search for <strong data-start="2702" data-end="2729">derived infrastructures</strong>: models that preserve obstruction classes by gluing local contexts via homotopy colimits rather than collapsing them into low-dimensional vectors.</p>
<hr data-start="2880" data-end="2883">
<p data-start="2885" data-end="3167" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to also add a <strong data-start="2917" data-end="2939">worked toy example</strong> (say, three documents and two queries) that shows explicitly how a single-vector embedding collapses distinct relations while a sheaf/hocolim construction would preserve them? That could make the abstract mapping very concrete.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9