ta-start="51" data-end="87">Alternatives to Embedding Models</strong> section into an RSVP-structured format:</p>
<hr data-start="131" data-end="134">
<h3 data-start="136" data-end="201">Appendix F.1: Retrieval Architectures Compared Through RSVP</h3>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="203" data-end="2134" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="203" data-end="419"><tr data-start="203" data-end="419"><th data-start="203" data-end="225" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="205" data-end="219">Model Type</strong></th><th data-start="225" data-end="241" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="227" data-end="240">Mechanism</strong></th><th data-start="241" data-end="273" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="243" data-end="272">RSVP Φ (Semantic Density)</strong></th><th data-start="273" data-end="314" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="275" data-end="313">RSVP 𝒗 (Vector Flow / Negentropy)</strong></th><th data-start="314" data-end="351" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="316" data-end="350">RSVP S (Entropy / Obstruction)</strong></th><th data-start="351" data-end="384" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="353" data-end="383">Category-Theoretic Analogy</strong></th><th data-start="384" data-end="400" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="386" data-end="399">Strengths</strong></th><th data-start="400" data-end="419" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="402" data-end="417">Limitations</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="635" data-end="2134"><tr data-start="635" data-end="1029"><td data-start="635" data-end="666" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="637" data-end="665">Single-Vector Embeddings</strong></td><td data-start="666" data-end="712" data-col-size="md">Collapse entire input into one dense vector</td><td data-start="712" data-end="767" data-col-size="md">Over-compressed: local meaning collapsed into global</td><td data-start="767" data-end="815" data-col-size="md">Flow bottlenecked—only one channel per object</td><td data-start="815" data-end="861" data-col-size="md">Obstructions erased rather than metabolized</td><td data-start="861" data-end="908" data-col-size="md">Premature colimit (collapse of all sections)</td><td data-start="908" data-end="947" data-col-size="md">Compact, fast, scalable to web scale</td><td data-start="947" data-end="1029" data-col-size="md">Cannot represent high sign-rank relations; brittle under compositional queries</td></tr><tr data-start="1030" data-end="1363"><td data-start="1030" data-end="1051" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1032" data-end="1050">Cross-Encoders</strong></td><td data-start="1051" data-end="1103" data-col-size="md">Recompute pairwise query–doc relations on the fly</td><td data-start="1103" data-end="1138" data-col-size="md">Preserves full context per query</td><td data-start="1138" data-end="1190" data-col-size="md">Flow recalculated dynamically; maximally flexible</td><td data-start="1190" data-end="1231" data-col-size="md">Entropy externalized into compute cost</td><td data-start="1231" data-end="1276" data-col-size="md">Fiber product (direct pairwise evaluation)</td><td data-start="1276" data-end="1316" data-col-size="md">Exact relevance modeling; high recall</td><td data-start="1316" data-end="1363" data-col-size="md">Quadratic compute cost; infeasible at scale</td></tr><tr data-start="1364" data-end="1735"><td data-start="1364" data-end="1390" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1366" data-end="1389">Multi-Vector Models</strong></td><td data-start="1390" data-end="1443" data-col-size="md">Multiple vectors per document with MaxSim operator</td><td data-start="1443" data-end="1486" data-col-size="md">Moderately preserved: local patches kept</td><td data-start="1486" data-end="1530" data-col-size="md">Flow distributed across multiple channels</td><td data-start="1530" data-end="1565" data-col-size="md">Obstructions tracked in overlaps</td><td data-start="1565" data-end="1617" data-col-size="md">Homotopy colimit (gluing with overlaps preserved)</td><td data-start="1617" data-end="1672" data-col-size="md">Finer granularity; balances compactness and fidelity</td><td data-start="1672" data-end="1735" data-col-size="md">Still bounded in dimension; less tested for reasoning tasks</td></tr><tr data-start="1736" data-end="2134"><td data-start="1736" data-end="1771" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1738" data-end="1770">Sparse Models (BM25, SPLADE)</strong></td><td data-start="1771" data-end="1813" data-col-size="md">High-dimensional sparse lexical vectors</td><td data-start="1813" data-end="1849" data-col-size="md">Preserves raw lexical microstates</td><td data-start="1849" data-end="1903" data-col-size="md">Flow distributed but shallow; no entropic smoothing</td><td data-start="1903" data-end="1948" data-col-size="md">Stores entropy rather than metabolizing it</td><td data-start="1948" data-end="2012" data-col-size="md">Infinite-dimensional limit (sheaf becomes trivially glueable)</td><td data-start="2012" data-end="2060" data-col-size="md">Strong performance on keyword/logical queries</td><td data-start="2060" data-end="2134" data-col-size="md">Weak for reasoning/instruction-following; less semantic generalization</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end" style="height: 48.7031px;"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065