<hr data-start="2136" data-end="2139">
<p data-start="2141" data-end="2253">This table makes clear that each architecture corresponds to a different <strong data-start="2214" data-end="2250">semantic infrastructure strategy</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="2254" data-end="2489">
<li data-start="2254" data-end="2300">
<p data-start="2256" data-end="2300"><strong data-start="2256" data-end="2273">Single-vector</strong> → premature compression.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2301" data-end="2362">
<p data-start="2303" data-end="2362"><strong data-start="2303" data-end="2321">Cross-encoders</strong> → recomputation at the cost of energy.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2363" data-end="2431">
<p data-start="2365" data-end="2431"><strong data-start="2365" data-end="2381">Multi-vector</strong> → local sections glued with preserved overlaps.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2432" data-end="2489">
<p data-start="2434" data-end="2489"><strong data-start="2434" data-end="2444">Sparse</strong> → entropy archival in infinite dimensions.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2491" data-end="2788">A genuine RSVP retrieval model would likely combine elements of all four: local section preservation (multi-vector), scalable compression (single-vector), dynamic recomputation when necessary (cross-encoder), and archival access (sparse), orchestrated under an entropy-aware balancing principle.</p>
<hr data-start="2790" data-end="2793">
<p data-start="2795" data-end="3032" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to sketch how such an <strong data-start="2835" data-end="2859">RSVP retrieval model</strong> could be mathematically formalized (e.g., as a functor with adaptive colimits that decide between compression, recomputation, or expansion depending on entropy thresholds)?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8