ata-start="0" data-end="182">Here’s a polished <strong data-start="18" data-end="41">paper-ready section</strong> you can drop into your draft. I’ve written it in academic prose with clear transitions so it fits alongside the other parts of your essay.</p>
<hr data-start="184" data-end="187">
<h2 data-start="189" data-end="266">7. Towards RSVP Retrieval: Adaptive Colimits for Semantic Infrastructure</h2>
<p data-start="268" data-end="800">The findings of Weller et al. (2025) on the inherent limits of single-vector embeddings provide an important boundary condition for the design of future retrieval systems. If embeddings necessarily collapse complex query–document relations into an underdetermined space, then the architecture of retrieval must move beyond uniform compression. In this section, we sketch an alternative retrieval paradigm inspired by the Relativistic Scalar Vector Plenum (RSVP) framework and its emphasis on entropy-aware semantic infrastructure.</p>
<h3 data-start="802" data-end="844">7.1 Embeddings as Premature Colimits</h3>
<p data-start="845" data-end="1321">Single-vector embedding models can be understood as enforcing a premature global section of the sheaf of query–document relations. By mapping entire contexts into a single <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^d</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8491em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">R</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8491em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">d</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> vector, they collapse obstruction classes that would otherwise indicate incompatible or overlapping local structures. This premature colimit is efficient but brittle: contradictions are erased rather than metabolized, leading to the combinatorial failures exposed by the LIMIT dataset.</p>
<h3 data-start="1323" data-end="1365">7.2 RSVP Fields as Control Variables</h3>
<p data-start="1366" data-end="1427">RSVP provides a natural language to diagnose this collapse.</p>
<ul data-start="1428" data-end="1779">
<li data-start="1428" data-end="1525">
<p data-start="1430" data-end="1525"><strong data-start="1430" data-end="1462"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span> (semantic density):</strong> overly compressed when reduced to a single embedding vector.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1526" data-end="1662">
<p data-start="1528" data-end="1662"><strong data-start="1528" data-end="1557"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>⃗</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec v</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.714em;"></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.714em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="accent-body" style="left: -0.2077em;"><span class="overlay" style="height: 0.714em; width: 0.471em;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="0.471em" height="0.714em" viewBox="0 0 471 714" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin" style="width: 0.471em;"><path d="M377 20c0-5.333 1.833-10 5.5-14S391 0 397 0c4.667 0 8.667 1.667 12 5
3.333 2.667 6.667 9 10 19 6.667 24.667 20.333 43.667 41 57 7.333 4.667 11
10.667 11 18 0 6-1 10-3 12s-6.667 5-14 9c-28.667 14.667-53.667 35.667-75 63
-1.333 1.333-3.167 3.5-5.5 6.5s-4 4.833-5 5.5c-1 .667-2.5 1.333-4.5 2s-4.333 1
-7 1c-4.667 0-9.167-1.833-13.5-5.5S337 184 337 178c0-12.667 15.667-32.333 47-59
