</li>
<li data-start="404" data-end="447">
<p data-start="406" data-end="447"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">3</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>: “Graph theory with DP subtask”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="448" data-end="481">
<p data-start="450" data-end="481"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_4</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">4</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>: “Sorting with heaps”</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="483" data-end="512">Now consider three queries:</p>
<ul data-start="513" data-end="700">
<li data-start="513" data-end="561">
<p data-start="515" data-end="561"><strong data-start="515" data-end="521">Q1</strong>: “Find all dynamic programming tasks”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="562" data-end="623">
<p data-start="564" data-end="623"><strong data-start="564" data-end="570">Q2</strong>: “Find problems that use both DP and graph search”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="624" data-end="700">
<p data-start="626" data-end="700"><strong data-start="626" data-end="632">Q3</strong>: “Find problems that share structure across alternating subtasks”</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="702" data-end="705">
<h4 data-start="707" data-end="748">Step 1: Initial pass (single-vector)</h4>
<ul data-start="749" data-end="994">
<li data-start="749" data-end="994">
<p data-start="751" data-end="783">The embedding model retrieves:</p>
<ul data-start="786" data-end="994">
<li data-start="786" data-end="830">
<p data-start="788" data-end="830">Q1 → {D1, D3} (correct, low obstruction)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="833" data-end="905">
<p data-start="835" data-end="905">Q2 → {D1, D2, D3} (ambiguous: D2 not really relevant, some collapse)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="908" data-end="994">
<p data-start="910" data-end="994">Q3 → {D1, D2, D3, D4} (completely blurred, cannot separate alternating structure).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start="996" data-end="1034">Step 2: Estimate obstruction load</h4>
<ul data-start="1035" data-end="1236">
<li data-start="1035" data-end="1066">
<p data-start="1037" data-end="1066"><strong data-start="1037" data-end="1043">Q1</strong>: Low <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="true">^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9233em;"></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9233em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span><span class="svg-align" style="width: calc(100% - 0.1667em); margin-left: 0.1667em; top: -3.6833em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span style="height: 0.24em;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="100%" height="0.24em" viewBox="0 0 1062 239" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path d="M529 0h5l519 115c5 1 9 5 9 10 0 1-1 2-1 3l-4 22
c-1 5-5 9-11 9h-2L532 67 19 159h-2c-5 0-9-4-11-9l-5-22c-1-6 2-12 8-13z"></path></svg></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1067" data-end="1136">
<p data-start="1069" data-end="1136"><strong data-start="1069" data-end="1075">Q2</strong>: Moderate <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="true">^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9233em;"></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9233em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span><span class="svg-align" style="width: calc(100% - 0.1667em); margin-left: 0.1667em; top: -3.6833em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span style="height: 0.24em;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="100%" height="0.24em" viewBox="0 0 1062 239" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path d="M529 0h5l519 115c5 1 9 5 9 10 0 1-1 2-1 3l-4 22
c-1 5-5 9-11 9h-2L532 67 19 159h-2c-5 0-9-4-11-9l-5-22c-1-6 2-12 8-13z"></path></svg></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (confusion between DP vs greedy).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1137" data-end="1236">
<p data-start="1139" data-end="1236"><strong data-start="1139" data-end="1145">Q3</strong>: High <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="true">^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9233em;"></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9233em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span><span class="svg-align" style="width: calc(100% - 0.1667em); margin-left: 0.1667em; top: -3.6833em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span style="height: 0.24em;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="100%" height="0.24em" viewBox="0 0 1062 239" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path d="M529 0h5l519 115c5 1 9 5 9 10 0 1-1 2-1 3l-4 22
c-1 5-5 9-11 9h-2L532 67 19 159h-2c-5 0-9-4-11-9l-5-22c-1-6 2-12 8-13z"></path></svg></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (no clean separation, resembles LIMIT-style combinatorial overlap).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start="1238" data-end="1258">Step 3: Routing</h4>
<ul data-start="1259" data-end="1602">
<li data-start="1259" data-end="1324">
<p data-start="1261" data-end="1324"><strong data-start="1261" data-end="1267">Q1</strong>: Obstruction low → stay with <strong data-start="1297" data-end="1314">single-vector</strong> output.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1325" data-end="1447">
<p data-start="1327" data-end="1447"><strong data-start="1327" data-end="1333">Q2</strong>: Moderate → escalate to <strong data-start="1358" data-end="1374">multi-vector</strong>, preserving local semantic patches. This separates {D1, D3} from {D2}.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1448" data-end="1602">
<p data-start="1450" data-end="1602"><strong data-start="1450" data-end="1456">Q3</strong>: High → route to <strong data-start="1474" data-end="1491">cross-encoder</strong> on ambiguous subset {D1–D4}, recomputing pairwise query–doc scores to recover correct alternating structure.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start="1604" data-end="1640">Step 4: Adaptive colimit gluing</h4>
<ul data-start="1641" data-end="1914">
<li data-start="1641" data-end="1776">
<p data-start="1643" data-end="1659">Merge outputs:</p>
<ul data-start="1662" data-end="1776">
<li data-start="1662" data-end="1690">
<p data-start="1664" data-end="1690">From single-vector (Q1).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1693" data-end="1731">
<p data-start="1695" data-end="1731">From multi-vector refinement (Q2).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1734" data-end="1776">
<p data-start="1736" data-end="1776">From cross-encoder recomputation (Q3).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1777" data-end="1914">
<p data-start="1779" data-end="1914">The homotopy colimit ensures overlaps are consistent across queries (e.g., D1 appears in both Q1 and Q2, but only in the right role).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1916" data-end="1919">
<p data-start="1921" data-end="1934"><strong data-start="1921" data-end="1932">Result:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1935" data-end="2036">
<li data-start="1935" data-end="1952">
<p data-start="1937" data-end="1952">Q1 → {D1, D3}</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1953" data-end="1987">
<p data-start="1955" data-end="1987">Q2 → {D1, D3} (no spurious D2)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1988" data-end="2036">
<p data-start="1990" data-end="2036">Q3 → {D2, D4} (correct alternating subtasks)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2038" data-end="2041">
<p data-start="2043" data-end="2186">This toy example dramatizes the <strong data-start="2075" data-end="2105">adaptive colimit principle</strong>: keep things cheap if possible, but escalate only when obstruction demands it.</p>
